name issue_150_gcc_v2_high_jitter
describe 3 Mbps link, 40 ms jitter with reordering, every v2 switch on: the target libwebrtc's GoogCC holds there (issue #150)
# `high_jitter` with every v2 switch on, the configuration PR #116 makes the default.
# Root cause: SendHistory::OnFeedback reported a packet again each time `tcc v2`'s generator re-reported it
# (libwebrtc's TransportFeedbackAdapter erases a received packet from its history, so a second report fails the lookup).
# The repeated, earlier receive times moved the acked-bitrate window backwards, which resets it, so the first
# acknowledged rate arrived after the first overuse and AimdRateControl halved the 1116 kbps probe result twice in 50 ms.
# Seed 1, main 4dbe631: cc.target_avg_kbps 503, cc.utilization_pct 19.5, video.avg_kbps 323.
# Seeds 1-10 after the fix: cc.utilization_pct 29-65 (mean 41.7), video.avg_kbps 478-1008 (mean 669), cc.queue_p95_ms 7-24.
# libwebrtc (parity-data, 10 seeds): cc.utilization_pct 25-48 (mean 37.1), video.avg_kbps 400-742 (mean 584), queue p95 1-8 ms.
# The lines below lock the level reached on seeds 1-5.
# Target (issue #150): cc.target_avg_kbps, cc.utilization_pct, video.avg_kbps and cc.queue_p95_ms within the parity band of libwebrtc.
# Fixed (acked-rate estimator as libwebrtc's RobustThroughputEstimator): seeds 5 and 10 no longer run away, see issue_150_gcc_v2_high_jitter_seed{5,10}.
cc v2
pacer v2
tcc v2
rtx v2
rtcp v2
keyframe v2
allocator v2
packetization v2
audio v2
duration 30s
at 0s capacity=3000kbps delay=30ms jitter=40ms reorder=on queue=300ms
expect audio.interruptions == 0
expect video.freeze_count == 0
expect cc.utilization_pct >= 30
expect video.avg_kbps >= 450
expect cc.queue_p95_ms < 40
